Changes code from Helium's helium/core/services-prefs.patch, services-schema-nag.patch and onboarding-page.patch
(GPL-3.0, The Helium Authors).

Settings has no Helium services page: no route (chrome://settings/privacy/services opens Settings itself), no view,
and no "set up services" button that opened chrome://setup, which isn't built. Helium services stay off in Ardia
(the branding patch, which also removes its row), so the page could only offer switches that do nothing.

